//
// The design artifacts' Menu PANEL: an opaque OVERLAY surface (it floats above
// the window's own blur, so it never blurs) — surfaceOverlay, a 1 px glassEdge,
// shadow3 and the lit top line, radius 16, padding 4 — holding `WinMenuItem`
// rows (radius 12 = 16 − 4, concentric), `WinMenuRow` headers and
// `WinMenuDivider`s. `width` in px: 220 when omitted, 240 for the ⋮ app menu.
// The panel eats its own taps (`WinNoop`) so a press on its padding or a
// divider never reaches the backdrop that closes the menu.
//
// Where it opens is the caller's: `WinAppWindow`'s `appMenu` slot anchors the
// ⋮ app menu under its button (bottom-end, submenus flying out to the left);
// a submenu is a second `WinMenu` beside the row that opened it (its first row
// level with that row), and that row keeps its `selected` layer while open.
//
// STORE CONTRACT (the consuming app declares these — the kit dispatches):
//   events  WinNoop

Component WinMenu {
    props: {
        width: Int,
    }
    slot items
    Stack {
        Slot items
    }
    .gap(0)
    .padding(4)
    .width(220)
    .minWidth($props.width)
    .maxWidth($props.width)
    .material(overlay)
    .rounded(lg)
    on Tap -> dispatch(WinNoop)
}

// A menu divider: 1 px `separator`, inset 8 from the panel's sides, 4 above
// and below.
Component WinMenuDivider {
    Stack {
        Stack { }
            .height(1)
            .bg(separator)
    }
    .paddingY(4)
    .paddingX(8)
}
